{:edb/db-before-t 2382 :edb/db-after-t 2383 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535695 50 #inst "2026-10-09T05:22:24.578Z" 13194139535695 true] [17592186096587 1020 #edb/ref 17592186361726 13194139535695 true] [17592186096587 1020 #edb/ref 17592186361736 13194139535695 true] [17592186096588 1020 #edb/ref 17592186361718 13194139535695 true] [17592186096589 1020 #edb/ref 17592186361729 13194139535695 true] [17592186288689 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361725 13194139535695 true] [17592186361718 1017 #edb/ref 17592186361719 13194139535695 true] [17592186361718 1089 "q-114703" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361718 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535695 true] [17592186361718 1100 "$\\int ({sin}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x=$" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361718 1113 #uuid "39c87398-5175-5dc1-8cc4-8632b2bd67dc" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361718 1145 "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)={sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({sin}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361719 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361720 13194139535695 true] [17592186361719 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361721 13194139535695 true] [17592186361719 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361722 13194139535695 true] [17592186361719 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361723 13194139535695 true] [17592186361719 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361724 13194139535695 true] [17592186361719 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535695 true] [17592186361719 1041 "selection" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361719 1104 #edb/ref 17592186361724 13194139535695 true] [17592186361719 1110 #uuid "95f1b6f1-7c30-5049-8e29-bdaab28db919" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361720 1034 "x+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361720 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535695 true] [17592186361720 1111 #uuid "5c779221-1a96-5a0a-95ee-7ffce3e0d80e" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361721 1034 "2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361721 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535695 true] [17592186361721 1111 #uuid "c2b31554-f53c-5090-becd-84389075d104" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361722 1034 "-\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361722 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535695 true] [17592186361722 1111 #uuid "832ecd68-e9de-52d4-9dfa-2eb63d77df59" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361723 1034 "x-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361723 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535695 true] [17592186361723 1111 #uuid "f3d2adff-a695-526c-a7a8-eaa4be5da50e" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361724 1034 "\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361724 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535695 true] [17592186361724 1111 #uuid "b316147c-c6ef-56b7-b960-a1ebd09d2874" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361725 1034 "2\\pi" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361725 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535695 true] [17592186361725 1111 #uuid "f567a014-d677-5c69-85cf-f6da6014595b" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361726 1017 #edb/ref 17592186361727 13194139535695 true] [17592186361726 1089 "q-348755" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361726 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535695 true] [17592186361726 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069587/assets/e0a3fb0f4fc900f6ef8ac041ded7553f7ac44cc09f946bc3ebfee8a3235e8e94.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=5{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+2{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+1,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=0,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361726 1113 #uuid "d5e356de-7912-5bf7-8fed-9681512abebd" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361726 1145 "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(5{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+2{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+1)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nRecall  ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1,$ so we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+2{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+1 & =3{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+2({sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+{cos}^{2}⁡(2x))+1 \\\\  & =3{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1.\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(3{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(\\frac{3}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1)+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+\\frac{9}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{3}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\frac{9}{2}x)\\,|}_{-\\pi /2}^{0} \\\\  & =(\\frac{3}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡0+\\frac{9}{2}\\cdot 0)-(\\frac{3}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-2\\pi )+\\frac{9}{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =(0+0)-(0-\\frac{9\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361727 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361728 13194139535695 true] [17592186361727 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535695 true] [17592186361727 1041 "field-1" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361727 1104 #edb/ref 17592186361728 13194139535695 true] [17592186361727 1110 #uuid "f31cfdac-75c6-5bf0-a419-b8f355559f35" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361728 1034 "\\frac{9\\pi}{4}" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361728 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535695 true] [17592186361728 1111 #uuid "c0781bb8-a903-5df4-b276-c5f220c5aafc" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361729 1017 #edb/ref 17592186361730 13194139535695 true] [17592186361729 1089 "q-74407" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361729 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535695 true] [17592186361729 1100 "$\\int (3{x}^{2}+10{sin}^{2}⁡5x-10{cos}^{2}⁡5x)\\text{d}x=$" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361729 1113 #uuid "2d2caaa3-5720-58a5-a204-32175641ff19" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361729 1145 "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =5x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡10x={cos}^{2}⁡5x-{sin}^{2}⁡5x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3{x}^{2}+10{sin}^{2}⁡5x-10{cos}^{2}⁡5x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (3{x}^{2}-10({cos}^{2}⁡5x-{sin}^{2}⁡5x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (3{x}^{2}-10\\operatorname{cos}⁡10x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{3}-10(\\frac{1}{10}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x)+C \\\\  & ={x}^{3}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361730 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361731 13194139535695 true] [17592186361730 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361732 13194139535695 true] [17592186361730 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361733 13194139535695 true] [17592186361730 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361734 13194139535695 true] [17592186361730 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361735 13194139535695 true] [17592186361730 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535695 true] [17592186361730 1041 "selection" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361730 1104 #edb/ref 17592186361735 13194139535695 true] [17592186361730 1110 #uuid "7131b056-aaab-50e9-9652-3361506fe444" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361731 1034 "3-\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x+C" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361731 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535695 true] [17592186361731 1111 #uuid "842d857b-31f1-5712-a3a3-66b676c8fedd" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361732 1034 "{x}^{3}+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x+C" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361732 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535695 true] [17592186361732 1111 #uuid "ffbdfe91-1ce2-5b96-b7da-e9d6c5723d15" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361733 1034 "{x}^{3}-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x+C" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361733 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535695 true] [17592186361733 1111 #uuid "a34aa9e5-3650-562d-949b-cdba07b21c45" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361734 1034 "{x}^{3}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x+C" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361734 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535695 true] [17592186361734 1111 #uuid "c31474a9-e897-5e21-9dca-6d82f023f9ea" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361735 1034 "{x}^{3}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x+C" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361735 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535695 true] [17592186361735 1111 #uuid "bfcf3d1a-f70c-51a3-aea0-17346305b26d" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361736 1017 #edb/ref 17592186361737 13194139535695 true] [17592186361736 1089 "q-74408" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361736 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535695 true] [17592186361736 1100 "Calculate \n$\\int (5-8{cos}^{2}⁡2x)\\text{d}x.$" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361736 1113 #uuid "ff8c9059-4ccd-5c34-b361-0250f8da7c82" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361736 1145 "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1).\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =2x$, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡2x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (5-8{cos}^{2}⁡2x)\\text{d}x & =\\int [5-8\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1)]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int [5-4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1)]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (1-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x-4(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)+C \\\\  & =x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361737 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361738 13194139535695 true] [17592186361737 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361739 13194139535695 true] [17592186361737 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361740 13194139535695 true] [17592186361737 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361741 13194139535695 true] [17592186361737 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361742 13194139535695 true] [17592186361737 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535695 true] [17592186361737 1041 "selection" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361737 1104 #edb/ref 17592186361740 13194139535695 true] [17592186361737 1110 #uuid "16d79c9f-2069-5cd9-b62f-5a63f18b029f" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361738 1034 "5x-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+C" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361738 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535695 true] [17592186361738 1111 #uuid "88eef018-64bb-5b92-9c2f-1ec72b23190b" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361739 1034 "5x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+C" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361739 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535695 true] [17592186361739 1111 #uuid "0c9fa166-eeae-5071-b0a1-4bd3d34b9996" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361740 1034 "x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+C" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361740 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535695 true] [17592186361740 1111 #uuid "b5e0e150-4f95-50ed-81b8-24f3f0d94910" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361741 1034 "x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+C" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361741 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535695 true] [17592186361741 1111 #uuid "3c91618c-4258-5a14-8cd8-01e1586709c1" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361742 1034 "5x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+C" 13194139535695 true] [17592186361742 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535695 true] [17592186361742 1111 #uuid "46b5ef69-26de-5cc2-a63e-ea09ebba0936" 13194139535695 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-114703" 17592186361718 "q-114703/selection" 17592186361719 "q-114703/selection/0a5dac34e1924cc11131a63d7de27484b43e7b085d56f2b89ef8aa480eece498" 17592186361720 "q-114703/selection